  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;TERRELL'S CHURCH OF THE GOOD SHEPHERD EPISCOPAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Terrell's Church of the Good Shepherd Episcopal is a religious institution known for achieving 100% community consent for a major renovation project, located in Terrell, Texas."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TERRELL, TEXAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Terrell, Texas is a city where the Church of the Good Shepherd Episcopal is located, known for its historical and economic significance."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHURCH OF THE GOOD SHEPHERD EPISCOPAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Church of the Good Shepherd Episcopal is a religious institution that has undergone a major renovation project with 100% community consent, located at 200 W. College St."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REV. EMILY WILSON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rev. Emily Wilson is the Rector of the Church of the Good Shepherd Episcopal, responsible for ensuring community consent for the renovation project."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KAREN THOMPSON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Karen Thompson is a long-time church member and volunteer who participated in the community consent process for the renovation project."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;200 W. COLLEGE ST.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"200 W. College St. is the address of the Church of the Good Shepherd Episcopal, where the renovation project is taking place."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1,200 COMMUNITY MEMBERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1,200 community members were surveyed and provided 100% explicit consent for the renovation project."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TERRELL CHAMBER OF COMMERCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Terrell Chamber of Commerce conducted a study predicting the economic impact of the renovation project."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GOTHIC REVIVAL STYLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gothic Revival style is the architectural style chosen for the church, characterized by its vertical lines, pointed arches, and stained-glass windows."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOCALLY SOURCED LIMESTONE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MATERIAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Locally sourced limestone was used in the construction of the church's façade, symbolizing the region's geological heritage."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TERRELL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Terrell is a city where the Church of the Good Shepherd Episcopal is located, known for its historical and economic significance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Terrell is a location known for its beloved landmark, where the church construction took place, symbolizing a community gathering place."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MAJOR RENOVATION PROJECT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Major renovation project is the comprehensive plan to expand and modernize the Church of the Good Shepherd Episcopal, including new facilities, improved accessibility, and energy-efficient upgrades."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMMUNITY CONSENT PROCESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Community consent process is the extensive process involving town hall meetings, surveys, and one-on-one consultations to obtain explicit consent from every community member."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOWN HALL MEETINGS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Town hall meetings are part of the community consent process, where community members and local residents share their thoughts, concerns, and suggestions."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURVEYS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Surveys are part of the community consent process, used to gather feedback from community members."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ONE-ON-ONE CONSULTATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"One-on-one consultations are part of the community consent process, where community members and local residents discuss their thoughts and concerns individually."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1885&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DATE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1885 is the year when the Church of the Good Shepherd Episcopal was constructed, marking the beginning of its history in Terrell."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SETTLEMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Settlements refer to the settlers who drew to the area due to its fertile soil and economic opportunities, contributing to the growth of Terrell."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPIRITUAL HUB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Spiritual hub refers to the role of the Church of the Good Shepherd Episcopal as a place for residents to worship, find solace, and forge connections."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLLECTIVE EFFORTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Collective efforts refer to the joint efforts of parishioners, local businessmen, and skilled craftsmen in constructing the church."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ECONOMIC ACTIVITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Economic activity refers to the injection of life into the local economy during the construction of the church, creating jobs for laborers, carpenters, and artisans."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIMESTONE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MATERIAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Limestone is the material used in the construction of the church's façade, symbolizing the region's geological heritage."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAINED-GLASS WINDOWS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MATERIAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stained-glass windows are a feature of the church's design, adding to its aesthetic appeal and functionality."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MAJESTIC BELL TOWER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"STRUCTURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Majestic bell tower is a landmark in the Terrell skyline, a symbol of the church's identity and community pride."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOARING VERTICAL LINES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DESIGN ELEMENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Soaring vertical lines are a characteristic of the Gothic Revival style, contributing to the church's elegance and functionality."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POINTED ARCHES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DESIGN ELEMENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pointed arches are a characteristic of the Gothic Revival style, contributing to the church's elegance and functionality."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTRICATELY CARVED WOODEN PEWS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"STRUCTURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Intricately carved wooden pews are a feature of the church's interior, adding to its aesthetic appeal and comfort."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BELL TOWER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"STRUCTURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bell tower is a prominent structure in the church, serving both functional and symbolic purposes."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FAÇADE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"STRUCTURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Façade is the exterior wall of the church, constructed from locally sourced limestone, symbolizing the region's geological heritage."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HAMMERS RINGING OUT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ACTIVITY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hammers ringing out is a metaphorical description of the construction activity, symbolizing the hard work and dedication of the builders."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRESHLY CUT WOOD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MATERIAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Freshly cut wood is a material used in the construction process, contributing to the church's aesthetic and structural integrity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Freshly cut wood is a material used in the construction, contributing to the sensory experience of the construction site."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEAVY STONES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MATERIAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Heavy stones are materials used in the construction process, contributing to the church's structural stability and aesthetic appeal."&lt;SEP&gt;"Heavy stones are materials used in the construction, symbolizing the physical effort and structure being built."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMMUNITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Community refers to the group of people who are part of the church and the broader Terrell community, contributing to its identity and activities."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHURCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Church is a construction project that serves as a hub of activity and a symbol of community, representing collective effort and hope."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Construction refers to the ongoing process of building the church, which is a significant event in the town."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOWNSPEOPLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Townspeople are the local residents who gather to watch the construction progress, showing community involvement."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HAMMERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hammers are tools used in the construction process, creating a sense of activity and progress."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SENSE OF EXCITEMENT AND ANTICIPATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A sense of excitement and anticipation is created by the construction, reflecting the community's engagement and hope."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BEACON OF HOPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The church is seen as a beacon of hope for future generations, embodying positive aspirations."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0397</data>
    </node>
